PASS d5-3d: on the image of a duplication z -> (alpha z, beta z): q_2 = (alpha^2 + beta^2) q, sum_k E0^(k) = (|alpha|^2 + |beta|^2) E0, and the summed stress tensor T(alpha z) + T(beta z) = (|alpha|^2+|beta|^2) T(z); T(z) is duality invariant and obeys Rainich's identity (T eta)^2 = E0^2 1; at the equal split with relative duality angle theta, |q_2| = |cos theta| |q|
PASS d5-3e: X -> (cos(phi) X, sin(phi) R X) with R in U(3): the summed stress tensor is preserved for all X iff R is a duality rotation (T determines z z^* bijectively); q_2 iff R is real orthogonal; both iff R = +-1; and a G-linear W = U + iV preserving both E6 (+) E6 and q_2 has V = 0, since W^*W - W^T W = 2 V^T V - 2i V^T U
